# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=saved (coverage label only -- evening steers
# at no boss, the walk starts at the door same as any other) spec=druid:balance
# style=auto size=25 difficulty=heroic view=820x1180,touch save=carried
# (behaves as fresh per #273 -- the dev-server port is pid-derived so
# localStorage never actually carries across separate playbot invocations).
# #b=saved&s=25&h=1 unlocks the 25-heroic tier the same way every other
# 25-heroic carried-cell script in this ledger does.
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl first: druid:balance has one prior mode=walk
# appearance (2026-09-28T23:58:21Z, flee, 10-normal, 844x390 -- crossed THE
# VIGIL clean and killed two bosses pressing nothing at all). mode=walk +
# auto + 25-heroic has three prior appearances (mage:frost/1280x800,
# druid:feral/844x390, hunter:marksmanship/844x390) but never on the
# 820x1180 portrait-touch viewport, and never with a balance druid --
# a ranged caster spec like mage:frost, but a different autocast rotation
# and range band. Two questions open: does the 820x1180 layout hold up
# across a real multi-room evening the way it has in single-pull sessions,
# and does auto's known no-steering gap (2026-09-29's marksmanship finding:
# a fixed opening position can land inside a dead zone between a range bonus
# and an ability's own shorter cast range) show up on a different spec's own
# range thresholds.
open #b=saved&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:druid:balance
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start
targets
ui
evening auto 200 12
